Here is the commit message:
udevadm info: "-a" should enumerate sysfs attributes, not
 envs (#11642)

This fixes a bug introduced by 13aca847695f49afeb93367ecdad76035fa6c139.

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the use of `FOREACH_DEVICE_PROPERTY` to enumerate device properties instead of using `FOREACH_DEVICE_SYSATTR`, which led to the incorrect enumeration of environment variables rather than sysfs attributes when the `-a` option was used with `udevadm info`. This change in the iteration logic did not align with the intended functionality of the command, resulting in the bug.

Here is the patch:

 static void print_all_attributes(sd_device *device, const char *key) {
         const char *name, *value;

-        FOREACH_DEVICE_PROPERTY(device, name, value) {
+        FOREACH_DEVICE_SYSATTR(device, name) {
                 size_t len;

                 if (skip_attribute(name))
                         continue;

+                if (sd_device_get_sysattr_value(device, name, &value) < 0)
+                        continue;
+
                 /* skip any values that look like a path */
                 if (value[0] == '/')
                         continue;

                 /* skip nonprintable attributes */
                 len = strlen(value);
                 while (len > 0 && isprint(value[len-1]))
                         len--;
                 if (len > 0)
                         continue;

                 printf("    %s{%s}==\"%s\"\n", key, name, value);
         }
         puts("");
 }



